From 9f747e896cc1eabdd1c13af5deea8a733986773e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI_Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:17:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm-cuda: TF_GLM_DFLASH2_Q32, the drafter's 4-bit linears at
 32 groups (the reference engine's granularity)

M1's weight diff: the 64-group quantizer owns the drafter-fidelity gap (relrms 0.090 vs the reference 0.078).
This is M2: tf_glm_quantize4_32, the GS 32 tile of tf_pack_dense, the LaneTile<32,...> instantiation, the 32-wide
group sums, and the loader branch, behind TF_GLM_DFLASH2_Q32 (default off: every existing path byte-identical).
The output head keeps its 64 groups this revision (its sums come from the shared glue rmsnorm); scratch and the
weight buffer size for either. Drafts only propose: replies are the target's at either setting.
